					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7624123#post-4001459</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7624123/a-transcribed-collection-of-haiku-graffiti-from-site-42#post-4001459</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 24 Sep 2018 04:57:23 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Gabriel Jade</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>414239</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>“When composing a verse let there not be a hair's breath separating your mind from what you write; composition of a poem must be done in an instant, like a woodcutter felling a huge tree or a swordsman leaping at a dangerous enemy.”<br /> <strong>― Bashō</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>A collection of several haiku I've written since returning to the site. I won't list the inspiring articles here, though I'll gladly confirm/deny anyone that wants to take a stab at them.</p> <p>A sincere thank you to the entire SCP community, for making this old creepypasta hangout into such an awesome, creative place.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
